    "notes": [
      "EN: 10 kohm to 3V3 and 1 uF to GND so the supply settles before the chip starts; a reset button to GND.",
      "Firmware download over UART0 (TXD0, RXD0) from a USB-serial bridge; auto-reset: the bridge's DTR and RTS drive EN and IO0 through two transistors (the DevKitC circuit).",
      "Keep IO12 low at power-up; JTAG: IO14 TMS, IO12 TDI, IO13 TCK, IO15 TDO."
    ],
    "page": "9 peripheral schematics (figure 9, p. 39); 4 boot configurations (table 4)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Supply: 3.0-3.6 V able to deliver 500 mA (Wi-Fi TX peaks); 22 uF and 100 nF at the 3V3 pin.",
    "Strapping pins sampled at reset: IO0 (pull-up; low = download), IO2 (pull-down), IO12 MTDI (pull-down; high breaks boot with 3.3 V flash), IO15 MTDO (pull-up), IO5 (pull-up). Do not load them so they read wrong at reset.",
    "IO34, IO35, SENSOR_VP (GPIO36) and SENSOR_VN (GPIO39) are input only, without pull-ups. ADC2 is not usable while Wi-Fi runs: use ADC1 (IO32-IO39) for analog.",
    "Antenna: the top 6.19 mm of the module. The footprint keeps tracks, vias, pours and other parts out of it (0.5 mm margin). Espressif's hardware design guidelines recommend the antenna outside the base board or at its edge with the board cut away under it, and 15 mm clearance around it: place the module at a board edge with the antenna overhanging it (`place = [edge(.top, overhang = 6mm)]`).",
    "The EPAD (pin 39) to ground with thermal vias improves heat flow; it is optional, and too much paste lifts the module."
  ],
